# Issues first

Development tasks and ideas start as a GitHub issue on this repo. Do not implement a new feature, test plan, or process change until there is an issue (or you are creating it in the same turn).

- Open or reuse an issue, then a `feature/` / `fix/` branch, then a PR into `develop`.
- Issue title and body stay English. Say what to do and how we will know it is done.
- Link the PR to the issue (`Closes #N` or `Refs #N`).

## Foreign GitHub repos

If the user points at another GitHub repo as a reference, treat it as private inspiration.

- Do **not** put that URL, owner, or repo name in issues, PR titles/bodies, commit messages, README, or comments.
- Write the requirement in our words (`scripted window tests on every PR`, `split model canary`).
- Do not add “like &lt;other project&gt;” even without a link.

Attribution that already lives in `NOTICE` / `README` stays there. Do not spread it.